**Corollary 2.** If $n\in T$, let $q$ be the integer such that $s(n)=nq$. Then
$$
15(15^n-1)=14n(1+14q),
$$
and consequently
$$
n\mid 15(15^n-1).
$$

**Proof.** Lemma 1 gives
$$
15^{\,n+1}-14n-15=196nq,
$$
which rearranges to the displayed identity. The factor $14n$ then gives the divisibility. ∎

